  "solution": {
    "text": "Novolac on heating with formaldehyde undergoes cross-linking to form an infusible solid mass called Bakelite.&nbsp;It is a thermosetting polymer that cannot be reused or remoulded.&nbsp;&nbsp;Bakelite is used for making combs, phonograph records, electrical switches, and handles of various utensils",
